<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Merged into the generated app Info.plist by Tauri.

	  Voice mode (ADR 2026-07-31) is the only reason ZAM touches the microphone.
	  Both keys are mandatory, not advisory: macOS terminates the process
	  outright when SFSpeechRecognizer.requestAuthorization or AVAudioRecorder
	  runs in a bundle that lacks the matching usage description. That is also
	  why the device tier cannot be exercised from a bare `cargo test` binary —
	  only from the signed bundle.

	  The wording is what the learner reads in the consent sheet, so it names
	  what actually happens rather than the API being called.
	-->
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>ZAM uses the microphone only while voice mode is running, so you can answer your review cards out loud.</string>

	<!--
	  With the "device only" and "device first" preferences, recognition runs
	  entirely on this Mac and no audio is sent anywhere. Choosing "best
	  quality" in ZAM's settings sends the recording to the transcription model
	  you configured there.
	-->
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>ZAM turns your spoken answers into text so it can compare them with the expected answer. This happens on your Mac unless you choose a cloud model in ZAM's settings.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
